{
 "title": "Parameters and results",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "Functions can call each other; the result of one function can be an argument of another. `return` leaves the function at once, so it is also used for an **early return**."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "fn square(x: i32) -> i32:",
    "    return x * x",
    "",
    "fn abs_value(x: i32) -> i32:",
    "    if x < 0:",
    "        return -x",
    "    return x",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    print(square(abs_value(-4)))"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "16"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "Functions that return `bool` read like questions (`is_even`, `is_positive`) and fit nicely inside `if`."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "fn is_even(n: i32) -> bool:",
    "    return n % 2 == 0",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    for i in 1..=4:",
    "        if is_even(i):",
    "            print(i, \"is even\")",
    "        else:",
    "            print(i, \"is odd\")"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "1 is odd",
    "2 is even",
    "3 is odd",
    "4 is even"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "exercise",
   "id": "c03-l02-x1",
   "prompt": "Write `max_of(a, b)`: it returns the bigger one.",
   "starter": [
    "fn max_of(a: i32, b: i32) -> i32:",
    "    return 0",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    print(max_of(7, 12))",
    "    print(max_of(30, 4))"
   ],
   "solution": [
    "fn max_of(a: i32, b: i32) -> i32:",
    "    if a > b:",
    "        return a",
    "    return b",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    print(max_of(7, 12))",
    "    print(max_of(30, 4))"
   ],
   "hint": "Return `a` if `a > b`, otherwise return `b`.",
   "expected": [
    "12",
    "30"
   ]
  },
